    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 20th November 2006, the erection of a single storey part side/rear infill extension with 2.475m width, 2.40m high rising to meet the house at 3.40m high, 4.70m depth, was lawful within the meaning of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:\r\nThe development falls inside the provisions of Schedule 2, Part 1, Class B of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995 because the total cubic volume of the existing extensions combined with the proposed extension has a volume of under 15% of the cubic volume of the original house.\r\n"
